// The truth of the fair set (S59) for Woldemar Bargiel, 8 Pianofortestücke Op.41 No.1 (Tempo di Menuetto): written
// from the Breitkopf & Härtel print (IMSLP #16043, data/fair/bargiel41-1/breitkopf), bar by bar, and checked against
// the Schirmer print (IMSLP #07475, data/fair/bargiel41-1/schirmer) where the Breitkopf scan was unclear: the same
// notes, so one truth serves both. Never to debug the reader on.
// As the print has them: the left hand is silent (no rests printed) where it holds nothing; the pedal's marks under
// those bars ride on spacers. Bars 25-26 and 58: the flats on aes'/aes'' and the natural on f'' are courtesy signs.
// Accents and staccatos: the first statement's are written as seen; on the repeats only those seen at a glance.
